 3300. " term="202201"><period actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="5" building="" days="mon,tue,thu,fri" ends="10:50AM" max_waitlist="20" professor="Raymond Page" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="Raymond Page" room="Fuller Labs 320 " seats="54" section="AL01" starts="10:00AM" type="Lecture"/><period actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="0" building="" days="wed" ends="2:50PM" max_waitlist="0" professor="Raymond Page" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="Raymond Page" room="Atwater Kent 014 BME Lab " seats="18" section="AX03" starts="1:00PM" type="Lab"/></section><section actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="4" crn="000000334811334812" max_waitlist="0" number="BL01/BX01" part-of-term="B Term" seats="18" sec_desc=" Cat. I  Students are guided through the open-ended, real-world, design process starting with the project definition, specification development, management, team interactions and communication, failure and safety criteria, progress reporting, marketing concepts, documentation and technical presentation of the final project outcome. The course will include a significant writing component, will make use of computers, and hands-on design explorations.  Students who have previously received credit for BME 2300 may not receive credit for BME 3300. " term="202201"><period actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="17" building="" days="mon,tue,thu,fri" ends="9:50AM" max_waitlist="20" professor="Solomon Mensah" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="Solomon Mensah" room="Salisbury Labs 402 " seats="54" section="BL01" starts="9:00AM" type="Lecture"/><period actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="4" building="" days="wed" ends="10:50AM" max_waitlist="0" professor="Solomon Mensah" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="Solomon Mensah" room="Atwater Kent 014 BME Lab " seats="18" section="BX01" starts="9:00AM" type="Lab"/></section><section actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="3" crn="000000334811334809" max_waitlist="0" number="BL0