ics sequence that serves as a foundation for other courses in mechanical engineering. The course covers general two- and three-dimensional force and couple systems, distributed loads, resultant forces, moments of forces, free body diagrams, equilibrium of particles and finite sized bodies. Specific topics include friction, trusses, shear forces, bodies subjected to distributed loads, bending moments in beams, and first and second moments of plane areas. Recommended background: Differential (MA 1021) and integral (MA 1022) calculus, vector algebra (MA 1023), and double and triple integration (MA 1024). " max-credits="3.0" min-credits="3.0" name="Introduction To Static Systems" number="2501"><section actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="0" crn="000000334672334674" max_waitlist="0" number="AL01/AD01" part-of-term="A Term" seats="100" sec_desc=" Cat. I This is an introductory course in the engineering mechanics sequence that serves as a foundation for other courses in mechanical engineering. The course covers general two- and three-dimensional force and couple systems, distributed loads, resultant forces, moments of forces, free body diagrams, equilibrium of particles and finite sized bodies. Specific topics include friction, trusses, shear forces, bodies subjected to distributed loads, bending moments in beams, and first and second moments of plane areas. Recommended background: Differential (MA 1021) and integral (MA 1022) calculus, vector algebra (MA 1023), and double and triple integration (MA 1024). " term="202201"><period actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="0" building="" days="mon,tue,thu,fri" ends="3:50PM" max_waitlist="50" professor="Adam Powell" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="Adam Powell" room="Unity Hall 400 " seats="100" section="AL01" starts="3:00PM" type="Lecture"/><period actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="0" building="" days="wed" ends="3:50PM" max_waitlist="0" professor="Adam Powell" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="A