vector algebra (MA 1023), and double and triple integration (MA 1024). " term="202201"><period actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="77" building="" days="mon,tue,thu,fri" ends="8:50AM" max_waitlist="20" professor="Not Assigned" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="Not Assigned" room="Washburn 229 " seats="90" section="DL01" starts="8:00AM" type="Lecture"/><period actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="77" building="" days="wed" ends="9:50AM" max_waitlist="0" professor="Not Assigned" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="Not Assigned" room="Washburn 229 " seats="90" section="DD01" starts="8:00AM" type="Discussion"/></section><section actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="49" crn="000000337370337369" max_waitlist="0" number="DL02/DD02" part-of-term="D Term" seats="90" sec_desc=" Cat. I  This is an introductory course in the engineering mechanics sequence that serves as a foundation for other courses in mechanical engineering. The course covers general two- and three-dimensional force and couple systems, distributed loads, resultant forces, moments of forces, free body diagrams, equilibrium of particles and finite sized bodies. Specific topics include friction, trusses, shear forces, bodies subjected to distributed loads, bending moments in beams, and first and second moments of plane areas.  Recommended background: Differential (MA 1021) and integral (MA 1022) calculus, vector algebra (MA 1023), and double and triple integration (MA 1024). " term="202201"><period actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="49" building="" days="mon,tue,thu,fri" ends="11:50AM" max_waitlist="20" professor="Yihao Zheng" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="Yihao Zheng" room="Salisbury Labs 115 Kinnicutt Hall " seats="90" section="DL02" starts="11:00AM" type="Lecture"/><period actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="49" building="" days="wed" ends="12:50PM" max_waitlist="0" professor="Yihao Zheng" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="Yihao Zheng" room="Salisbury Labs 115 Kinnicutt Hall " seats="90" section="DD02" starts="11:00AM" type="Discussion"/></section></course><course course_desc=" Cat. I  This is an introductory course that addresses the analysis of basic mechanical and structural elements. Topics include general concepts of stresses, strains, and material properties of common engineering materials. Also covered are two-dimensional stress transformations, principal stresses, Mohr’s circle and deformations due to mechanical and thermal effects. Applications are to uniaxially loaded bars, circular shafts under torsion, bending and shearing and deflection of beams, and buckling of columns. Both statically determinate and indeterminate problems are analyzed.  Recommended background; mechanical systems (ES 2501 or equivalent), differential (MA 1021) and integral (MA 1022) calculus, vector algebra (MA 1023), and double and triple integration (MA 1024). " max-credits="3.0" min-credits="3.0" name="Stress Analysis" number="2502"><section actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="20" crn="000000334224334309" max_waitlist="0" number="AL01/AD01" part-of-term="A Term" seats="90" sec_desc=" Cat. I  This is an introductory course that addresses the analysis of basic mechanical and structural elements. Topics include general concepts of stresses, strains, and material properties of common engineering materials. Also covered are two-dimensional stress transformations, principal stresses, Mohr’s circle and deformations due to mechanical and thermal effects. Applications are to uniaxially loaded bars, circular shafts under torsion, bending and shearing and deflection of beams, and buckling of columns. Both statically determinate and indeterminate problems are analyzed.  Recommended background; mechanical systems (ES 2501 or equivalent), differential (MA 1021) and integral (MA 1022) calculus, vector algebra (MA 1023), and double and triple integration (MA 1024). " term="202201"><period actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="20" building=