ntals of heat transfer in the three modes of conduction, convection, and radiation. Topics include steady-state and transient heat conduction, forced external and internal convection, natural convection, heat exchanger analysis, radiation properties, and radiative exchange between surfaces.  Recommended background: knowledge of thermodynamics, fluid mechanics, and ordinary differential equations (ES 3001, ES 3004, and MA 2051) or equivalents. " term="202201"><period actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="21" building="" days="tue,fri" ends="3:50PM" max_waitlist="20" professor="Nicholas Dembsey" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="Nicholas Dembsey" room="Olin Hall 107 " seats="90" section="CL01" starts="2:00PM" type="Lecture"/><period actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="21" building="" days="wed" ends="12:50PM" max_waitlist="0" professor="Nicholas Dembsey" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="Nicholas Dembsey" room="Olin Hall 107 " seats="90" section="CD01" starts="12:00PM" type="Discussion"/></section><section actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="0" crn="000000337455337457" max_waitlist="0" number="DL01/DD01" part-of-term="D Term" seats="90" sec_desc=" Cat. I This course presents the fundamentals of heat transfer in the three modes of conduction, convection, and radiation. Topics include steady-state and transient heat conduction, forced external and internal convection, natural convection, heat exchanger analysis, radiation properties, and radiative exchange between surfaces. Recommended background: knowledge of thermodynamics, fluid mechanics, and ordinary differential equations (ES 3001, ES 3004, and MA 2051) or equivalents. " term="202201"><period actual_waitlist="5" availableseats="0" building="" days="tue,fri" ends="10:50AM" max_waitlist="20" professor="James Urban" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="James Urban" room="Unity Hall 500 " seats="90" section="DL01" starts="9:00AM" type="Lecture"/><period actual_waitlist="0" av