"><period actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="15" building="" days="wed" ends="4:50PM" max_waitlist="0" professor="Kristin Boudreau; David DiBiasio" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="Kristin Boudreau; David DiBiasio" room="Innovation Studio 105 Active Learning Classroom " seats="40" section="CL09 - GPS: Humanitarian Engineering" starts="3:00PM" type="Lecture"/><period actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="15" building="" days="mon,thu" ends="2:50PM" max_waitlist="0" professor="Kristin Boudreau; David DiBiasio" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="Kristin Boudreau; David DiBiasio" room="Innovation Studio 105 Active Learning Classroom " seats="40" section="CD09 - GPS: Humanitarian Engineering" starts="2:00PM" type="Discussion"/></section></course><course course_desc=" (1/12 unit) This course is open to all students who are undecided about or are thinking about changing their academic major. Students will conduct a self-assessment utilizing career assessment tools, research majors of interest and career paths, attend major panels, speak to students/faculty in majors of interest, and participate in informational interviews with alumni. Students will meet individually with Peer Advisors and/or a CDC staff member at least three times throughout the course. " max-credits="0.75" min-credits="0.75" name="Discovering Majors And Careers" number="1800"><section actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="10" crn="000000000000334560" max_waitlist="0" number="A01" part-of-term="A Term" seats="30" sec_desc=" (1/12 unit) This course is open to all students who are undecided about or are thinking about changing their academic major. Students will conduct a self-assessment utilizing career assessment tools, research majors of interest and career paths, attend major panels, speak to students/faculty in majors of interest, and participate in informational interviews with alumni. Students will meet individually with Peer Advisors and/or a CDC staff member at least three times throughout the course. " term="202201"><period actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="10" building="" days="wed" ends="12:50PM" max_waitlist="0" professor="Stefano DeAngelis; Amanda Laungani" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="Stefano DeAngelis; Amanda Laungani" room="Unity Hall " seats="30" section="A01" starts="12:00PM" type="Lecture"/></section><section actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="30" crn="000000000000336336" max_waitlist="0" number="C01" part-of-term="C Term" seats="30" sec_desc=" (1/12 unit) This course is open to all students who are undecided about or are thinking about changing their academic major. Students will conduct a self-assessment utilizing career assessment tools, research majors of interest and career paths, attend major panels, speak to students/faculty in majors of interest, and participate in informational interviews with alumni. Students will meet individually with Peer Advisors and/or a CDC staff member at least three times throughout the course. " term="202201"><period actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="30" building="" days="wed" ends="12:50PM" max_waitlist="0" professor="Not Assigned" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="Not Assigned" room="Unity Hall " seats="30" section="C01" starts="12:00PM" type="Lecture"/></section></course></dept><dept abbrev="GE" name="Geology"><course course_desc=" Cat. I  Students of this course will examine the fundamental principles of physical geology including the materials, structures, and surface features of the earth and the processes which produced them. Emphasis will be placed on the interrelationship of people and environment and applications to various fields of technology. The course includes field trips and a significant laboratory component. " max-credits="3.0" min-credits="3.0" name="Geology" number="2341"><section actual_waitlist="1" availableseats="0" crn="000000000000334411" max_waitlist="20" number="A01" part-of-term="A Term" seats="120" sec_desc=" Cat. I