urse may be offered as Writing Intensive (WI). " term="202201"><period actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="22" building="" days="mon,thu" ends="8:20PM" max_waitlist="0" professor="Not Assigned" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="Not Assigned" room="Salisbury Labs 105 " seats="30" section="D06 - SOC SCI RES-IQP: France" starts="6:30PM" type="Lecture"/></section><section actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="30" crn="000000000000337968" max_waitlist="0" number="D07 - SOC SCI RES-IQP- Boston, MA" part-of-term="D Term" seats="30" sec_desc=" Cat. I This course is open to students accepted to off-campus IQP centers and programs . The course introduces students to research design, methods for social science research, and analysis . It also provides practice in specific research and field skills using the project topics students have selected in conjunction with sponsoring agencies . Students learn to develop social science hypotheses based upon literature reviews in their topic areas and apply concepts drawn from social psychology, anthropology, sociology, economics and other areas as appropriate . Students make presentations, write an organized project proposal, and develop a communication model for reporting their project findings . Some sections of this course may be offered as Writing Intensive (WI). " term="202201"><period actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="30" building="" days="mon,thu" ends="8:20PM" max_waitlist="0" professor="Not Assigned" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="Not Assigned" room="Salisbury Labs 305 " seats="30" section="D07 - SOC SCI RES-IQP- Boston, MA" starts="6:30PM" type="Lecture"/></section><section actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="30" crn="000000000000337970" max_waitlist="0" number="D08 - SOC SCI RES-IQP- Farm Stay, MA" part-of-term="D Term" seats="30" sec_desc=" Cat. I This course is open to students accepted to off-campus IQP centers and programs . The course introduces students to research design, methods for 