d: mechanisms (ME 3310, ME 3311), stress analysis (ES 3502), design (ME 3320), thermo-fluids (ES 3001, ES 3003, ES 3004), materials (ES 2001), manufacturing (ME 1800). " max-credits="3.0" min-credits="3.0" name="Advanced Engineering Design" number="4320"><section actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="0" crn="000000334563334568" max_waitlist="0" number="AL01/AX01" part-of-term="A Term" seats="40" sec_desc=" Cat. I This course integrates students’ background in ME in a one-term design project that is usually taken from a local company. Students must organize themselves and the project to successfully realize a product that meets customer needs. Activities include problem definition, design analysis, mathematical modelling, CAD modelling, manufacturing, testing, liaison to vendors, customer relations, marketing, technical management, purchasing, report writing, and oral presentations. Recommended background: mechanisms (ME 3310, ME 3311), stress analysis (ES 3502), design (ME 3320), thermo-fluids (ES 3001, ES 3003, ES 3004), materials (ES 2001), manufacturing (ME 1800). " term="202201"><period actual_waitlist="9" availableseats="0" building="" days="mon,tue,fri" ends="10:50AM" max_waitlist="20" professor="Joe Stabile" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="Joe Stabile" room="Higgins Labs 230 Geom Modeling Computer Lab " seats="40" section="AL01" starts="10:00AM" type="Lecture"/><period actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="0" building="" days="thu" ends="11:50AM" max_waitlist="0" professor="Joe Stabile" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="Joe Stabile" room="Higgins Labs 230 Geom Modeling Computer Lab " seats="40" section="AX01" starts="10:00AM" type="Lab"/></section><section actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="10" crn="000000335020335022" max_waitlist="0" number="BL01/BX01" part-of-term="B Term" seats="40" sec_desc=" Cat. IThis course integrates students’ background in ME in a one-term designproject that is usually taken from a local company. Students must organizethemselves and the project to successfully realize a product that meets customerneeds. Activities include problem definition, design analysis, mathematicalmodelling, CAD modelling, manufacturing, testing, liaison to vendors,customer relations, marketing, technical management, purchasing, reportwriting, and oral presentations.Recommended background: mechanisms (ME 3310, ME 3311), stressanalysis (ES 3502), design (ME 3320), thermo-fluids (ES 3001, ES 3003,ES 3004), materials (ES 2001), manufacturing (ME 1800). " term="202201"><period actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="10" building="" days="mon,tue,thu,fri" ends="4:50PM" max_waitlist="10" professor="Pradeep Radhakrishnan" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="Pradeep Radhakrishnan" room="Higgins Labs 218 Discovery Classroom " seats="40" section="BL01" starts="4:00PM" type="Lecture"/><period actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="10" building="" days="wed" ends="4:50PM" max_waitlist="0" professor="Pradeep Radhakrishnan" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="Pradeep Radhakrishnan" room="Higgins Labs 218 Discovery Classroom " seats="40" section="BX01" starts="4:00PM" type="Lab"/></section><section actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="0" crn="000000336717336794" max_waitlist="0" number="CL01/CX01" part-of-term="C Term" seats="40" sec_desc=" Cat. IThis course integrates students’ background in ME in a one-term designproject that is usually taken from a local company. Students must organizethemselves and the project to successfully realize a product that meets customerneeds. Activities include problem definition, design analysis, mathematicalmodelling, CAD modelling, manufacturing, testing, liaison to vendors,customer relations, marketing, technical management, purchasing, reportwriting, and oral presentations.Recommended background: mechanisms (ME 3310, ME 3311), stressanalysis (ES 3502), design (ME 3320), thermo-fluids (ES 3001, ES 3003,ES 3004), materials (ES 2001), manufacturing (ME 