required. " term="202201"><period actual_waitlist="7" availableseats="12" building="" days="mon,tue,thu,fri" ends="10:50AM" max_waitlist="10" professor="Lucy Caplan" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="Lucy Caplan" room="Alden Hall B06 Janet Earle Room " seats="25" section="D01" starts="10:00AM" type="Lecture"/></section></course><course course_desc=" MU 1100 Foundations of Music Theory and Aural Skills (1/3 unit; Cat. I) This course introduces basic music theory concepts and helps students develop aural skills. Course topics include scales, intervals, chords, harmonic progressions, and rhythm. Activities include both written work in music notation and ear training exercises. Recommended Background: some basic knowledge of reading music " max-credits="3.0" min-credits="3.0" name="Foundations of Music Theory and Aural Skills" number="1100"><section actual_waitlist="1" availableseats="0" crn="000000000000333979" max_waitlist="10" number="A01" part-of-term="A Term" seats="25" sec_desc=" MU 1100 Foundations of Music Theory and Aural Skills (1/3 unit; Cat. I) This course introduces basic music theory concepts and helps students develop aural skills. Course topics include scales, intervals, chords, harmonic progressions, and rhythm. Activities include both written work in music notation and ear training exercises. Recommended Background: some basic knowledge of reading music " term="202201"><period actual_waitlist="1" availableseats="0" building="" days="mon,tue,thu,fri" ends="10:50AM" max_waitlist="10" professor="Monica Hatch Moysey" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="Monica Hatch Moysey" room="Alden Hall B06 Janet Earle Room " seats="25" section="A01" starts="10:00AM" type="Lecture"/></section><section actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="1" crn="000000000000333967" max_waitlist="0" number="A02" part-of-term="A Term" seats="25" sec_desc=" MU 1100 Foundations of Music Theory and Aural Skills (1/3 unit; Cat. I) This course introduces basic musi