read music. Permission of the instructor is necessary to register.  " term="202201"><period actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="998" building="" days="thu" ends="7:50PM" max_waitlist="0" professor="Pieter Struyk" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="Pieter Struyk" room="Alden Hall B19 Lora E. Spaulding Recital Hall " seats="999" section="S02" starts="7:00PM" type="Lecture"/></section></course><course course_desc=" ISU  Students electing to complete their Humanities and Arts Requirement in music may, for one of their five courses, undertake 1/3 unit (normally at 1/12 unit per term) of private vocal or instrumental instruction. (Supplemental ensemble work is also strongly recommended.) The student must receive prior approval by a member of the WPI music faculty, and the instruction must be beyond the elementary level. Lessons involve a separate fee. Note that the maximum of 1/3 unit credit for lessons may be earned in addition to 1/3 unit credit for performance (see condition A or B below). Additional work, either in performance or lessons, may be acknowledged on the WPI transcript but will carry no WPI credit. Private lessons: voice, piano, organ, winds, brass, strings, and percussion. " max-credits="0.0" min-credits="0.0" name="Independent Instruction (Lessons) in Music" number="2450"><section actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="0" crn="000000000000336007" max_waitlist="0" number="F01" part-of-term="A Term, B Term" seats="0" sec_desc=" ISU  Students electing to complete their Humanities and Arts Requirement in music may, for one of their five courses, undertake 1/3 unit (normally at 1/12 unit per term) of private vocal or instrumental instruction. (Supplemental ensemble work is also strongly recommended.) The student must receive prior approval by a member of the WPI music faculty, and the instruction must be beyond the elementary level. Lessons involve a separate fee. Note that the maximum of 1/3 unit credit for lessons may be earned in addition to 1/3 unit credit for performance (see condition A or B below). Additional work, either in performance or lessons, may be acknowledged on the WPI transcript but will carry no WPI credit. Private lessons: voice, piano, organ, winds, brass, strings, and percussion. " term="202201"><period actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="0" building="" days="?" ends="12:00PM" max_waitlist="0" professor="Joshua Rohde" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="Joshua Rohde" room="Unknown" seats="0" section="F01" starts="12:00PM" type="Independent Study"/></section><section actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="999" crn="000000000000337891" max_waitlist="0" number="S01" part-of-term="C Term, D Term" seats="999" sec_desc=" ISU  Students electing to complete their Humanities and Arts Requirement in music may, for one of their five courses, undertake 1/3 unit (normally at 1/12 unit per term) of private vocal or instrumental instruction. (Supplemental ensemble work is also strongly recommended.) The student must receive prior approval by a member of the WPI music faculty, and the instruction must be beyond the elementary level. Lessons involve a separate fee. Note that the maximum of 1/3 unit credit for lessons may be earned in addition to 1/3 unit credit for performance (see condition A or B below). Additional work, either in performance or lessons, may be acknowledged on the WPI transcript but will carry no WPI credit. Private lessons: voice, piano, organ, winds, brass, strings, and percussion. " term="202201"><period actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="999" building="" days="?" ends="12:00PM" max_waitlist="0" professor="Joshua Rohde" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="Joshua Rohde" room="Unknown" seats="999" section="S01" starts="12:00PM" type="Independent Study"/></section></course><course course_desc=" MU 2501: Conducting (1/6 unit or 0 unit per semester depending on grading option; Cat. I)  This course will introduce students to the basic elements of conducting, such as gesture, music analysis, score preparation, and rehearsal techniques. Each section of the course is paired with a large ensemble to provide practical experience and opportunities between the areas of choral, band, orchestral, and jazz music. Course meeting times include during and outside of these set rehearsal times. Recommended Background: A basic reading knowledge of music and simultaneous enrollment in the corresponding large music ensemble " max-credits="1.5" min-credits="1.5" name="Conducting" number="2451"><section actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="952" crn="000000000000335697" max_waitlist="0" number="F01" part-of-term="A Term, B Term" seats="999" sec_desc=" MU 2501: Conducting (1/6 unit or 0 unit per semester depending on grading option; Cat. I)  This course will introduce students to the basic elements of conducting, such as gesture, music analysis, score preparation, and rehearsal techniques. Each section of the course is paired with a large ensemble to provide practical experience and opportunities between the areas of choral, band, orchestral, and jazz music. Course meeting times include during and outside of these set rehearsal times. Recommended Background: A basic reading knowledge of music and simultaneous enrollment in the corresponding large music ensemble " term="202201"><period actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="952" building="" days="thu" ends="6:30PM" max_waitlist="0" professor="Joshua Rohde" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="Joshua Rohde" room="First Baptist Church Gordon " seats="999" section="F01" starts="5:00PM" type="Lecture"/></section><section actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="952" crn="000000000000335696" max_waitlist="0" number="F02" part-of-term="A Term, B Term" seats="999" sec_desc=" MU 2501: Conducting (1/6 unit or 0 unit per semester depending on grading option; Cat. I)  This course will introduce students to the basic elements of conducting, such as gesture, music analysis, score preparation, and rehearsa