 Emphasis on topics and authors varies with the particular instructor. " term="202201"><period actual_waitlist="6" availableseats="-2" building="" days="mon,tue,thu,fri" ends="12:50PM" max_waitlist="10" professor="Adrien Stoloff" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="Adrien Stoloff" room="Higgins Labs 114 " seats="25" section="A04" starts="12:00PM" type="Lecture"/></section><section actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="2" crn="000000000000335036" max_waitlist="12" number="B01" part-of-term="B Term" seats="25" sec_desc=" Cat. IThis course provides an overview of key concepts, methods and authors in both fields. These introduce the student to the types of reasoning required for the pursuit of in-depth analysis in each discipline.Emphasis on topics and authors varies with the particular instructor. " term="202201"><period actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="2" building="" days="mon,tue,thu,fri" ends="11:50AM" max_waitlist="12" professor="Esther (Stella) Rosario" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="Esther (Stella) Rosario" room="Salisbury Labs 105 " seats="25" section="B01" starts="11:00AM" type="Lecture"/></section><section actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="0" crn="000000000000334693" max_waitlist="10" number="B02" part-of-term="B Term" seats="25" sec_desc=" Cat. I This course provides an overview of key concepts, methods and authors in both fields. These introduce the student to the types of reasoning required for the pursuit of in-depth analysis in each discipline. Emphasis on topics and authors varies with the particular instructor. " term="202201"><period actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="0" building="" days="mon,tue,thu,fri" ends="4:50PM" max_waitlist="10" professor="Not Assigned" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="Not Assigned" room="Salisbury Labs 011 " seats="25" section="B02" starts="4:00PM" type="Lecture"/></section><section actual_waitlist="1" availableseats="10" crn="000000000000336207" max_waitlist="10" number="C