h any level of yoga experience (including first timers) are welcome. " term="202201"><period actual_waitlist="8" availableseats="0" building="" days="mon,thu" ends="3:50PM" max_waitlist="10" professor="Kathryn Moncrief" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="Kathryn Moncrief" room="Recreation Center Dance " seats="25" section="D01" starts="3:00PM" type="Workshop"/></section><section actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="0" crn="000000000000337461" max_waitlist="10" number="D02" part-of-term="D Term" seats="15" sec_desc=" WPE 1612 Introductory Yoga Cat. I (1/12 unit) This yoga class focuses on connecting the mind, body, and spirit through an awareness of breath. Participating in yoga can improve core strength, flexibility, balance, mindfulness, and relaxation and decrease stress. Those with any level of yoga experience (including first timers) are welcome. " term="202201"><period actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="0" building="" days="tue,thu" ends="6:50PM" max_waitlist="10" professor="Meng Le" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="Meng Le" room="Daniels Hall 102E " seats="15" section="D02" starts="6:00PM" type="Workshop"/></section><section actual_waitlist="3" availableseats="0" crn="000000000000340287" max_waitlist="10" number="D03" part-of-term="D Term" seats="15" sec_desc=" WPE 1612 Introductory Yoga Cat. I (1/12 unit) This yoga class focuses on connecting the mind, body, and spirit through an awareness of breath. Participating in yoga can improve core strength, flexibility, balance, mindfulness, and relaxation and decrease stress. Those with any level of yoga experience (including first timers) are welcome. " term="202201"><period actual_waitlist="3" availableseats="0" building="" days="mon,thu" ends="5:50PM" max_waitlist="10" professor="Catherine Flayhan" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="Catherine Flayhan" room="Daniels Hall 102E " seats="15" section="D03" starts="5:00PM" type="Workshop"/></section></course><course course_desc=" WPE 1613: Succeeding as an Introvert (Pass/NR; 1/12units; Cat I) Does spending time in crowds or at a party wear you out? Do you enjoy time alone? Does the thought of working on a team make you nervous? Are you quiet around your classmates? Do you tend to avoid small talk or get tongue-tied in large groups? Would you rather think about a problem than discuss it with others? If you answered “yes” to several of these questions, this course is for you. Society puts a strong emphasis on extroversion, and those who frequently speak up get more attention and often advance professionally more quickly than their more reserved peers. Yet some of our greatest thinkers and leaders have been introverts. While the teamwork culture of WPI and most professions can present challenges to introverts, career success depends on the ability to work with others. This course will help introverted students learn to thrive at college and throughout their careers. Students will learn about the nature of introversion, including the strengths and challenges of being an introvert. Students will also learn personal and professional skills, such as how to successfully work on a team, present to an audience, manage their energy levels, and have difficult conversations with others. Grades will be Pass/NR. " max-credits="0.75" min-credits="0.75" name="Succeeding as an Introvert" number="1613"><section actual_waitlist="7" availableseats="0" crn="000000000000334972" max_waitlist="10" number="B01" part-of-term="B Term" seats="46" sec_desc=" WPE 1613: Succeeding as an Introvert (Pass/NR; 1/12units; Cat I) Does spending time in crowds or at a party wear you out? Do you enjoy time alone? Does the thought of working on a team make you nervous? Are you quiet around your classmates? Do you tend to avoid small talk or get tongue-tied in large groups? Would you rather think about a problem than discuss it with others? If you answered “yes” to several of these questions, this course is for you. Society puts a strong emphasis on extroversion, and those who frequently speak up get more attention and often advance professionally more quickly than their more reserved peers. Yet some of our greatest thinkers and leaders have been introverts. While the teamwork culture of WPI and most professions can present challenges to introverts, career success depends on the ability to work with others. This course will help introverted students learn to thrive at college and throughout their careers. Students will learn about the nature of introversion, including the strengths and challenges of being an introvert. Students will also learn personal and professional skills, such as how to successfully work on a team, present to an audience, manage their energy levels, and have difficult conversations with others. Grades will be Pass/NR. " term="202201"><period actual_waitlist="7" availableseats="0" building="" days="tue" ends="12:50PM" max_waitlist="10" professor="N. Aaron Deskins; Kristin Boudreau" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="N. Aaron Deskins; Kristin Boudreau" room="Innovation Studio 203 Active Learning Classroom South " seats="46" section="B01" starts="12:00PM" type="Workshop"/></section></course><course course_desc=" WPE 1699 Special Topics in Holistic Well-Being, Cat. I (1/12 unit) This course provides an opportunity for students to learn about a special topic in holistic wellbeing. The topics are subject to change on a rotating basis to provide flexibility in the offerings based upon student interest and the latest practice and science of well-being. " max-credits="0.75" min-credits="0.75" name="Special Topics in Holistic Well-Being" number="1699"><section actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="1" crn="000000000000333928" max_waitlist="5" number="A01 - ST in Holistic Well-Being:  Intuitive eating" part-of-term="A Term" seats="20" sec_desc=" WPE 1699 Special Topics in Holistic Well-Being, Cat. I (1/12 unit) This course provides an opportunity for students to learn about a special topic in holistic wellbeing. The topics are subject to change on a rotating basis to provide flexibility in the offerings based upon student interest and the latest practice and science of well-being. " term="202201"><period actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="1" building="" days="tue,thu" ends="10:50AM" max_waitlist="5" professor="Shavaun Cloran" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="Shavaun Cloran" room="Daniels Hall 102E " seats="20" section="A01 - ST in Holistic Well-Being:  Intuitive eating" starts="10:00AM" type="Workshop"/></section><section actual_waitlist="2" availableseats="0" crn="000000000000334256" max_waitlist="10" number="A02 - ST in Holistic Well-Being: Regenerative Cultures" part-of-term="A Term" seats="17" sec_desc=" WPE 1699 Special Topics in Holistic Well-Being, Cat. I (1/12 unit) This course provides an opportunity for students to learn about a special topic in holistic wellbeing. The topics are subject to change on a rotating basis to provide flexibility in the offerings based upon student interest and the latest practice and science of well-being. " term="202201"><period actual_waitlist="2" availableseats="0" building="" days="mon,thu" ends="12:50PM" max_waitlist="10" professor="Katherine Foo" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="Katherine Foo" room="Daniels Hall 102E " seats="17" section="A02 - ST in Holistic Well-Being: Regenerative Cultures" starts="12:00PM" type="Workshop"/></section><section actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="0" crn="000000000000333844" max_waitlist="10" number="A03 - ST in Holistic Well-Being: Sophomore Success-Navigating Your Second Year at WPI" part-of-term="A Term" seats="40" sec_desc=" WPE 1699 Special Topics in Holistic Well-Being, Cat. I (1/12 unit) This course provides an opportunity for students to learn about a special topic in holistic wellbeing. The topics are subject to change on a rotating basis to provide flexibility in the offerings based upon student interest