 availableseats="5" building="" days="mon,thu" ends="12:50PM" max_waitlist="5" professor="Not Assigned" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="Not Assigned" room="Daniels Hall 102E " seats="17" section="B02 - ST in Holistic Well-Being: Regenerative Cultures" starts="12:00PM" type="Workshop"/></section><section actual_waitlist="3" availableseats="0" crn="000000000000336172" max_waitlist="15" number="C01 - ST in Holistic Well-Being: Finding Joy in the Visual Arts" part-of-term="C Term" seats="18" sec_desc=" WPE 1699 Special Topics in Holistic Well-Being, Cat. I (1/12 unit) This course provides an opportunity for students to learn about a special topic in holistic wellbeing. The topics are subject to change on a rotating basis to provide flexibility in the offerings based upon student interest and the latest practice and science of well-being.  This course introduces students to the aesthetic benefits that works of visual art impart as a means to promote joy and well-being. Classes meet at the Worcester Art Museum, where focus on selected works of painting, sculpture, and other media from the collections will enhance the experience of perceiving qualities inherent in emotional responses to an artwork.   " term="202201"><period actual_waitlist="3" availableseats="0" building="" days="wed,fri" ends="12:50PM" max_waitlist="15" professor="Michelle Borowski" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="Michelle Borowski" room="Other " seats="18" section="C01 - ST in Holistic Well-Being: Finding Joy in the Visual Arts" starts="12:00PM" type="Workshop"/></section><section actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="10" crn="000000000000336171" max_waitlist="10" number="C02 - ST in Holistic Well-Being: Intuitive Eating" part-of-term="C Term" seats="20" sec_desc=" WPE 1699 Special Topics in Holistic Well-Being, Cat. I (1/12 unit) This course provides an opportunity for students to learn about a special topic in holistic wellbeing. The topics are subject to change on a rotating basis to provide flexibility in the offerings based upon student interest and the latest practice and science of well-being. " term="202201"><period actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="10" building="" days="tue,thu" ends="10:50AM" max_waitlist="10" professor="Shavaun Cloran" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="Shavaun Cloran" room="Daniels Hall 102E " seats="20" section="C02 - ST in Holistic Well-Being: Intuitive Eating" starts="10:00AM" type="Workshop"/></section><section actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="24" crn="000000000000336106" max_waitlist="10" number="C03 - ST in Holistic Well-Being: Sophomore Success-Navigating Your Second Year at WPI" part-of-term="C Term" seats="50" sec_desc=" WPE 1699 Special Topics in Holistic Well-Being, Cat. I (1/12 unit) This course provides an opportunity for students to learn about a special topic in holistic wellbeing. The topics are subject to change on a rotating basis to provide flexibility in the offerings based upon student interest and the latest practice and science of well-being. " term="202201"><period actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="24" building="" days="tue,fri" ends="10:50AM" max_waitlist="10" professor="Miriam Cohen" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="Miriam Cohen" room="Washburn 229 " seats="50" section="C03 - ST in Holistic Well-Being: Sophomore Success-Navigating Your Second Year at WPI" starts="10:00AM" type="Workshop"/></section><section actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="5" crn="000000000000337403" max_waitlist="10" number="D01 - ST in Holistic Well-Being: Exploring the Impact of Nutrition on Brain, Body and Planet" part-of-term="D Term" seats="20" sec_desc=" WPE 1699 Special Topics in Holistic Well-Being, Cat. I (1/12 unit) This course provides an opportunity for students to learn about a special topic in holistic wellbeing. The topics are subject to change on a rotating basis to provide flexibility in the offerings based upon student interest and the latest practice and science of well-being. " term="202201"><period actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="5" building="" days="tue,thu" ends="10:50AM" max_waitlist="10" professor="Shavaun Cloran" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="Shavaun Cloran" room="Daniels Hall 102E " seats="20" section="D01 - ST in Holistic Well-Being: Exploring the Impact of Nutrition on Brain, Body and Planet" starts="10:00AM" type="Workshop"/></section><section actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="0" crn="000000000000341738" max_waitlist="10" number="D02 - ST in Holistic Well-Being: Pranayama" part-of-term="D Term" seats="15" sec_desc=" WPE 1699 Special Topics in Holistic Well-Being, Cat. I (1/12 unit) This course provides an opportunity for students to learn about a special topic in holistic wellbeing. The topics are subject to change on a rotating basis to provide flexibility in the offerings based upon student interest and the latest practice and science of well-being. " term="202201"><period actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="0" building="" days="mon,thu" ends="12:50PM" max_waitlist="10" professor="Katherine Foo" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="Katherine Foo" room="Daniels Hall 102E " seats="15" section="D02 - ST in Holistic Well-Being: Pranayama" starts="12:00PM" type="Workshop"/></section><section actual_waitlist="1" availableseats="0" crn="000000000000344024" max_waitlist="10" number="F01 - ST in Holistic Well-Being: Strategies for College Learning and Productivity" part-of-term="A Term, B Term" seats="30" sec_desc=" WPE 1699 Special Topics in Holistic Well-Being, Cat. I (1/12 unit)  Success in college requires more than just academic proficiency - it takes strong executive functioning skills to manage time, stay organized, and adapt to new academic challenges. This course provides students with practical strategies to enhance their productivity, develop effective study habits, and improve self-regulation. Topics include time management, prioritization, note-taking methods, metacognition, motivation, self-advocacy, and stress management. Students will build confidence in their ability to navigate coursework, seek support when needed, and develop resilience in the face of setbacks. By the end of the course, students will leave with a personalized toolkit for academic success.  " term="202201"><period actual_waitlist="1" availableseats="0" building="" days="wed" ends="2:50PM" max_waitlist="10" professor="Amy Curran; Lauren Buffone" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="Amy Curran; Lauren Buffone" room="Salisbury Labs 305 " seats="30" section="F01 - ST in Holistic Well-Being: Strategies for College Learning and Productivity" starts="2:00PM" type="Workshop"/></section></course><course course_desc="" max-credits="0.75" min-credits="0.75" name="Varsity Football Team" number="2001"><section actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="926" crn="000000000000334076" max_waitlist="0" number="A01" part-of-term="A Term" seats="999" sec_desc="" term="202201"><period actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="926" building="" days="?" ends="12:00PM" max_waitlist="0" professor="Christopher Robertson" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="Christopher Robertson" room="Unknown" seats="999" section="A01" starts="12:00PM" type="Workshop"/></section><section actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="930" crn="000000000000335168" max_waitlist="0" number="B01" part-of-term="B Term" seats="999" sec_desc="" term="202201"><period actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="930" building="" days="?" ends="12:00PM" max_waitlist="0" professor="Not Assigned" professor_email="look@it.up" professor_sort_name="Not Assigned" room="Unknown" seats="999" section="B01" starts="12:00PM" type="Workshop"/></section></course><course course_desc="" max-credits="0.75" min-credits="0.75" name="Varsity Men's Soccer Team" number="2002"><section actual_waitlist="0" availableseats="988" crn="000000000000334048" max_waitlist="0" number="A01" part-of-term="A Term" seats="999" sec_desc="